owing{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mengcar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mengcar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mengcar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mengcar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mengcar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mengcar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mengcar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-18T09:49:54Z","updated_at":"2026-08-18T09:49:54Z","body":"@antekjb I'd like to pick this up after #141415 merges, if it's available. \n\nFrom my understanding this and others in #141411 are related, but depend on #141403? I learned about these issues from @macsko following the last SIG scheduling meeting (thank you). This would be my first contribution to k/k so any advice and adjustments would be welcomed :)\n\nConfirming the scope: `NoteLengthLimit` is the only symbol `pkg/scheduler` uses from `k8s.io/kubernetes/pkg/apis/core/validation`. `validation.NoteLengthLimit` is referenced exactly once, inside `truncateMessage` in `pkg/scheduler/schedule_one.go`. That function has one production caller and two in `schedule_one_test.go`.\n\nIt's defined as `NoteLengthLimit = 1024` in`pkg/apis/core/validation/events.go`, and the scheduler and that file are its only two users in the whole repo.\n\nOn the comments in the issue description: I couldn't find an obvious existing location suitable for it in staging. `component-helpers/scheduling` exists, but the constant is an Events API validation limit rather than a scheduling concept, so putting it there doesn't seem right.\n\nI think it would be reasonable to have it as a local const in `pkg/scheduler`, with a comment recording that a local copy is safe since the value can only grow.\n\nThanks in advance and appreciate patience while I'm still learning."